                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Initially was a fan of the game, but as I got further into it, it started to feel less like a puzzle game, and more like a really complicated maze. Visual and audio are great though, as you can plainly see from the trailer.\n\nI never really had any \"problem solving\" moments, it just felt like I was solving a line maze using the classic brute force method... AKA just hugging 1 side of the maze wall until you reach the end\n\n\nAnd that is basically what the gameplay started to turn into as I got further, albeit more complicated with switches, and rotations, moving platforms, etc.\n\nThere were no real \"aha\" moments, it was usually just finding myself stumbling into the solution after exhausting all possible paths and being like \"oh okay, i guess that was it\". I could never really visualize the problem/solution process like with other puzzle games.",
